er four points to be covered by two sunny lines.\n\n6. **Conclusion.**  \n   The non‑sunny line must contain at least two points (Step 3), but every such possibility is ruled out by Lemma 2. Therefore a configuration with exactly two sunny lines cannot exist for \\(n=3\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{No configuration exists for }n=3\\text{ with }k=2\\text{ sunny lines.}}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
